So my priest was doing very well in this game, found the quest and the
castle easy enough, though a little boring from all the repetitive
combat. (I was wielding +4 Frostbane and it was actually taking me a
while to kill all those undead creatures.) Sorting through my stuff in
preparation for Gehennom, I realized I had a wand of polymorph, a =oPC,
and an amulet of unchanging, and decided to cut down on the monotony of
the mazes by doing Gehennom as a Xorn.  I had spells of magic mapping
and detect treasure, so this would really mean I could zip through each
level.  So I polyied in to a Xorn, and was a little disturbed to find
how low my HP were, even after boosted by a few potions of full
healing.  On the other hand, I was delighted to see that I was now
getting four times as many attacks per turn as before.  No more the
annoyance of long battles just to kill a wraith.  Most everything went
down in two turns, and if necessary, it was easy to retreat through a
wall, taking off my shield, cast a healing spell, and come back
swinging.

Thus I reached Juiblex's swamp.  Juiblex -- yeah, yeah -- down in two
turns.  I was levitating my way across the swamp, HP at about 80, when
I saw a j next to me.  Lazily, I swung at it.  And, to my horrow, saw:

